bianbu-agent-memory (0.1.13) unstable; urgency=medium

  * 修复 MCP 子进程读不到 Runtime 主机上下文：FastMCP 把 tools/call 的
    `_meta` 以 pydantic `Meta` 模型交给工具，`bianbu/host` 落在
    `model_extra` 里。原来的读取只在 `isinstance(meta, Mapping)` 分支内回退到
    `model_extra`，既不是 Mapping 的模型永远读不到，session/run/agent/account
    全是空串；AgentMemory 于是带空 session 落证据，被 memoryd 判
    `invalid evidence references`，MCP 写入静默失败。
  * 写入失败不再一律折叠成 `backend_unavailable`：memoryd 的拒绝按真实错误码
    返回（如 `invalid_argument`）并带原因，`memory_record` 的返回文本也给出
    后端结论，避免「写入被拒」与「后端不可用」混为一谈。
  * 证据 ID 按 memoryd 的标识符规则生成：空值或非法字符（含超长）时不再发非法
    evidence，而是照常记录该条记忆但不带会话证据；未受 Runtime 管理的调用方不会
    再因证据字段整条写失败。
  * 修复 Worker 注册连接被提前关闭：`WorkerRegistration.open()` 原来在
    `with socket.socket(...)` 里建连接，返回即关闭，broker 按 EOF 删注册项，
    子进程刚注册就被静默注销。改为由实例持有连接，测试断言 broker 侧看不到
    EOF。

 -- liudecheng <decheng.liu@spacemit.com>  Tue, 15 Sep 2026 18:25:00 +0800

bianbu-agent-memory (0.1.12) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Ship an MCP server in the Python SDK:
    `bianbu_agent_sdk.memory.mcp_server` exposes the AgentMemory tools
    (`memory`, `memory_record`, `memory_retrieve`, `session_search`) over
    stdio via `python -m bianbu_agent_sdk.memory.mcp_server`, so the Runtime's
    bianbu.memory plugin can serve them as an MCP server instead of directory
    Tools. New optional extra `mcp` pins `mcp>=1.9,<2`.
  * The server reads its execution context from the Runtime: `_meta` on
    `tools/call` carries the session/run/agent/account scope, and
    `BIANBU_MEMORY_REGISTRATION_SOCKET` points at the Control-attested broker
    that pins this process' memoryd registry entry for its whole lifetime.
    Identity stays with memoryd's SO_PEERCRED verification; neither input is
    an authorization input.
  * Destructive `remove` mints its own one-shot confirmation token from
    `/etc/bianbu-agent-memory/adapter-confirmation.secret`, so deleting a
    memory needs no extra operator configuration once the Runtime has asked
    the user for approval.

 -- Bianbu Agent Team <bianbu-agent@spacemit.com>  Tue, 15 Sep 2026 17:00:00 +0800

bianbu-agent-memory (0.1.9) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Enable semantic indexing out of the box: the embedding defaults now ship
    enabled, base_url http://127.0.0.1:18801/v1, model qwen3-embedding-0.6b.
    The three values move together because validate_config requires an
    endpoint + model when enabled and a missing base_url silently disables
    the client.
  * Upgrade semantics: config files without an embedding section (or with
    partial sections) backfill from the new defaults via serde(default) and
    activate semantic indexing. Devices where the model has not landed yet
    keep the graceful lexical-only degradation (MEM-NFR-02); background
    indexing defers instead of failing. Explicit disabled sections keep
    embedding off, and the settings-page toggle remains the opt-out.
  * New AGENT_MEMORY_EMBEDDING_DISABLED=1 environment escape hatch suppresses
    only the out-of-the-box default (same pattern as AGENT_MEMORY_CACHE_KB):
    it keeps test suites hermetic when a real server listens on the default
    port, and gives operators a config-free kill switch. Explicit embedding
    sections are unaffected. Run the workspace tests with it set when a live
    embedding server is present.

 -- Bianbu Agent Team <bianbu-agent@spacemit.com>  Sat, 12 Sep 2026 23:10:00 +0800

bianbu-agent-memory (0.1.8) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Decouple the indexing timeout from the interactive retrieval budget:
    new embedding.index_timeout_ms (default 10000, 100..=600000) drives the
    background backfill batches and the post-commit single-record embed,
    while max_latency_ms stays the search-only budget (clamped to 1500 ms).
    With the old shared 1500 ms default, 32-record batches on the K3 CPU
    (~2.5 s) pushed large spaces into permanent ServerUnavailable retries.
  * Ship the embedding model downloader (bibit-intent house pattern):
    /usr/libexec/bianbu-agent-memory-download-embedding-model fetches the
    Qwen3-Embedding-0.6B Q8_0 GGUF from the vendor model_zoo with
    retry/resume and size + sha256 verification against the pinned release
    hash.
  * postinst starts the download as a background best-effort job, logs to
    /var/log/bianbu-agent-memory-model-download.log, and enables + starts
    the ConditionPathExists-gated embedding unit once the verified model
    lands. Semantic indexing stays opt-in via embedding.enabled.
  * memoryd unit StateDirectoryMode 0700 -> 0750: systemd re-enforces the
    state directory mode on every start, silently overriding the postinst's
    0750 and locking the embedding unit (User=bianbu) out of models/ after
    any memoryd restart. Sensitive files keep their own 0600/0700.

